- `src/renderer/main.js`: replaced the last lazy
  `require('./controllers/playback-controller')` inside the `createGetter`
  thunk with a hoisted static `import PlaybackController from
  './controllers/playback-controller'`, so the thunk is now the same
  one-liner shape as the other eight. No `.default` access anywhere.
- Files changed: `src/renderer/controllers/torrent-list-controller.js`,
  `src/renderer/controllers/playback-controller.js`,
  `src/renderer/main.js`, `src/renderer/controllers/AGENTS.md`,
  `specs/prd.json`, `progress.log`.
- **Tests:** no test was written. There is still no unit test runner for
  renderer modules (that is US-019), and this is a pure
  module-format change with no behaviour to assert. Evidence came from
  the launch check plus a targeted runtime probe instead (below).
- `npm test` (standard + depcheck) passes. `npm run build` compiles all
  64 files.
- **Verification:** launched via `npx electron --no-sandbox .` after
  `npm run build`. App reached `'Main Window'` and `init: 745ms`, and a
  `did-finish-load` probe reported
  `{hasHeader: true, selectionChanged: true, restored: true,
  previewSet: 0.5, previewCleared: true}` -- i.e. both converted
  controllers loaded, constructed, and handled real dispatches.
- **Smoke test NOT run.** The six-step manual smoke test needs an
  interactive session. The acceptance criterion calls out the torrent
  row context menu, torrent delete, and video playback start/stop;
  those three specifically were not exercised, because each is either
  blocking (native menu) or destructive (delete) or needs real media.
  The residual risk is concentrated in
  `TorrentListController.openTorrentContextMenu`, which is the only
  path in the two files that touches `remote.Menu` -- and it is
  untouched apart from the import line.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - **`electron.remote.getCurrentWindow()` in `src/renderer/main.js`
    (lines 145, 406, 418) already throws at runtime on master.** It
    logs `Uncaught (in promise) TypeError: Cannot read properties of
    undefined (reading 'getCurrentWindow')` -- `electron.remote` was
    removed from Electron; the working module is `@electron/remote`,
    which the controllers import correctly. This is PRE-EXISTING (I
    confirmed it by `git stash`-ing my diff, rebuilding, and relaunching
    the baseline, which logs the same error). Do not mistake it for
    breakage introduced by an ESM conversion, and do not fix it here --
    it belongs to the Phase 2 window/shim work (US-024).
  - When probing the renderer, remember **torrent selection lives on
    `state.selectedInfoHash`, not on a `selected` flag on the torrent
    object**. Reading `torrent.selected` returns `undefined` and makes a
    working dispatch look like a no-op.
